<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Campbell (missionary)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1766–<a href="/years/1840">1840</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Campbell was a Scottish minister who twice inspected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a>'s stations in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. In 1813 he helped the people at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griquatown">Klaarwater</a> adopt a written constitution and renamed the place Griquatown. On his second journey in 1820 he visited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahurutshe">Bahurutshe</a> town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaditshwene">Kaditshwene</a> and described its size, metalwork and trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-campbell-missionary.jpg" alt="John Campbell (missionary)" width="320" height="576" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Campbell (1766-1840) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Campbell_(missionary)02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
